# Supabase Realtime — the LIVE PUSH channel for dispatch, unit status and the maps.
#
# PUSH IS THE PRIMARY CHANNEL FOR DISPATCH — SET THESE.
#
# Polling is a bounded fallback so a dropped connection degrades instead of going dark, not
# an equivalent alternative. On a dispatch surface, instant vs "up to 20-30 seconds" is an
# operational difference, so treat an unconfigured push channel as something to fix.
#
# The app WILL still run with these unset and will not crash — that is deliberate (a dispatch
# surface must never white-screen over a config problem) and it is what makes a self-host
# without Supabase Realtime possible. It is not what makes it advisable.
#
# BOTH ARE REQUIRED TOGETHER. If either is missing, Realtime stays off (the client
# needs the pair to construct). Both values are public by design — the anon key grants
# no data access on its own; the authz'd REST API remains the source of truth and
# Broadcast messages are only treated as "refetch now" signals.
#
# ⚠ THESE ARE THE *CLIENT* VARS, AND THEY ARE NOT THE SAME AS THE SERVER'S
# SUPABASE_URL / SUPABASE_ANON_KEY. The server ones let OpenFirehouse PUBLISH
# broadcasts; these let the browser SUBSCRIBE to them. You need both halves for live
# push. Setting only the server pair is a silent no-op in the browser — that mistake
# is exactly how push was lost on our own production for 34 days.
#
# Find these in your Supabase project: Settings → API → Project URL + anon/public key.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR_PROJECT_REF.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your_anon_public_key

# Cloudinary — photo/video uploads
VITE_CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME=your_cloud_name
VITE_CLOUDINARY_UPLOAD_PRESET=openfirehouse

# Web Push — VAPID public key (safe to expose; private key lives on server only)
VITE_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=BHKUp3EaGG-Ro7Ja4aubygmOfWrs32ia55Nept8l2I655ciPrvREtjWurKmb4zmgRjqtt24L5FRTz9PhGqsWafQ
